cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "TrainDoctor: An executable RL environment for debugging and repairing distributed ML training failures"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khanna
    given-names: Tarang
repository-code: "https://github.com/TarangKhanna/traindoctor-env"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
abstract: >-
  An environment in which an agent diagnoses and repairs a failed multi-rank
  PyTorch/Gloo training job, with a verifier that re-executes the proposed
  repair in a disposable sandbox and checks that training recovered with its
  computation intact (committed-sample accounting, restored checkpoint,
  optimizer and sampler state, rank consistency), not merely that the job
  exits cleanly. Two task families are included; the exploratory RL results and the
  red-team audit of the verifier are in traindoctor-research and were not
  independently reviewed.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - RL environment
  - LLM agents
  - distributed training
  - verifiers
